-- Migration: 0015_intent_events_session_id_fix
-- FOLLOW-286 (LG-1 + LG-2): Fix intent_events join-key and event_type vocabulary.
--
-- LG-2 fix: Rename `intent_session_id` to `session_id`.
--
--   The 0014 DDL wrote a SHA-256→UUID-v4 derived value into `intent_session_id` (via
--   `deriveSessionUuid()` in the CF Worker handler). The corresponding Postgres table
--   `intent_sessions.id` is generated by `gen_random_uuid()` — the two values never
--   match, making the documented FK join (FOLLOW-269 replay) always return empty results.
--
--   Fix: the column is renamed from `intent_session_id` to `session_id` and the handler
--   now writes the RAW `session_id` string (the SDK anonymous session fingerprint, e.g.
--   a SHA-256 hex string). FOLLOW-269 replay queries must join on:
--     intent_events.session_id = intent_sessions.session_id
--     AND intent_events.tenant_id = intent_sessions.tenant_id
--   (composite text key, not the UUID surrogate `intent_sessions.id`).
--
--   This decision is recorded here per AC4 of FOLLOW-286.
--
-- LG-1 fix: Extend the event_type vocabulary to include 'intent.snapshot'.
--
--   The 0014 DDL documented the LowCardinality vocabulary as:
--     'quiz_answer' | 'chat_turn' | 'behavioral' | 'dwell' | 'pageview' | 'referrer' | 'finalized'
--   The ingest handler (FOLLOW-266 Phase 2) writes `event_type = 'intent.snapshot'`, which
--   was outside the documented vocabulary. ClickHouse LowCardinality(String) does NOT enforce
--   a constraint (any string is accepted), but the mismatch would silently break FOLLOW-269
--   GROUP BY queries that filter on the 0014 vocabulary.
--
--   Fix: `'intent.snapshot'` is added to the documented vocabulary. The shared constant
--   `INTENT_SNAPSHOT_EVENT_TYPE` in `@estalara/shared` pins both sides so they cannot
--   diverge again.
--
--   Full vocabulary after this migration:
--     'quiz_answer' | 'chat_turn' | 'behavioral' | 'dwell' | 'pageview' |
--     'referrer' | 'finalized' | 'intent.snapshot'
--
-- Idempotent: RENAME COLUMN is supported by ClickHouse MergeTree only via ALTER TABLE.
--   ClickHouse Cloud supports ALTER TABLE … RENAME COLUMN since 23.x.
--   If the column has already been renamed (re-apply), this will error; wrap in a
--   separate migration or apply once per environment.

ALTER TABLE intent_events RENAME COLUMN intent_session_id TO session_id;
